OL,3,GNEWSAFly-tippers to be fined five times
OL,4,Amore than before
OL,5,
OL,6,FFly-tippers in a town are facing a big
OL,7,Fjump in fines - from #1,000 to #5,000.
OL,9,FSwindon Borough Council says it wants
OL,10,Fto "send a very clear message" to
OL,11,Fpeople who dump things like mattresses,
OL,12,Ffurniture and household waste around
OL,13,Fthe town.
OL,15,FKevin Parry, cabinet member for
OL,16,Frecycling and streetscene, said:
OL,17,F"Fly-tipping is not a minor
OL,18,Finconvenience. It blights
OL,19,Fneighbourhoods, damages our environment
OL,20,Fand leaves ordinary taxpayers footing
OL,21,Fthe bill to clear up other people's
OL,22,Fmess."
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
